  Concept 4: Conditions in TypeScript
1. if statement
if ka matlab hai: agar condition true hai, tab code chalao.
Example:
let age: number = 24;

if (age >= 18) {
    console.log("You are eligible to vote");
}


Output:
You are eligible to vote


Kaise kaam karta hai?
1. age ki value 24 hai.
2. age >= 18 check hota hai.
3. Condition true hai.
4. Isliye if ke andar ka code execute hota hai.
Agar age 16 kar do, toh condition false hogi aur message print nahi hoga.
let age: number = 16;

if (age >= 18) {
    console.log("You are eligible to vote");
}


Output: kuch print nahi hoga.
2. if...else
Agar condition true ho toh ek kaam, warna doosra kaam.
let age: number = 16;

if (age >= 18) {
    console.log("Eligible");
} else {
    console.log("Not eligible");
}


Output:
Not eligible


Yaad rakhne ka formula:
- if → agar condition true hai.
- else → agar condition false hai.
3. if...else if...else
Jab multiple conditions check karni hon, tab else if use hota hai.
Example: Exam result.
let marks: number = 75;

if (marks >= 90) {
    console.log("Grade A");
} else if (marks >= 60) {
    console.log("Grade B");
} else if (marks >= 35) {
    console.log("Grade C");
} else {
    console.log("Fail");
}


Output:
Grade B


Kyun? Marks 75 hain. Pehli condition false hai, doosri condition true hai. Isliye Grade B print hoga aur baaki conditions check nahi hongi.
Dhyan do: conditions ka order important hai. Sabse high marks wali condition pehle check karna sahi rahega.
4. Logical operators ke saath conditions
Maan lo exam dene ke liye age 18 ya usse zyada honi chahiye aur ID card bhi hona chahiye.
let age: number = 22;
let hasId: boolean = true;

if (age >= 18 && hasId) {
    console.log("You can enter");
} else {
    console.log("Entry denied");
}


Output:
You can enter


&& ka matlab dono conditions true honi chahiye.
5. switch statement
Jab ek variable ki value ke hisaab se alag-alag cases handle karne hon, tab switch useful hota hai.
Example: Day number.
let day: number = 2;

switch (day) {
    case 1:
        console.log("Monday");
        break;

    case 2:
        console.log("Tuesday");
        break;

    case 3:
        console.log("Wednesday");
        break;

    default:
        console.log("Invalid day");
}


Output:
Tuesday


break current case ko execute karne ke baad switch se bahar nikalta hai. default tab execute hota hai jab koi case match nahi karta.

