Concept 5: Loops in TypeScript
1. Loop kya hota hai?
Maan lo tumhe "Hello" 5 baar print karna hai.
Loop ke bina:
console.log("Hello");
console.log("Hello");
console.log("Hello");
console.log("Hello");
console.log("Hello");


Loop ke saath:
for (let i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
    console.log("Hello");
}


Output dono mein same hoga:
Hello
Hello
Hello
Hello
Hello


Yaad rakho: Loop ka matlab hai kisi kaam ko baar-baar repeat karna.
2. for loop — sabse important
Pehle ye code samjho:
for (let i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
    console.log(i);
}


Output:
1
2
3
4
5


For loop ke 3 parts
let i = 1
Starting point — counting 1 se shuru hogi.

i <= 5
Condition — jab tak ye true hai, loop chalega.

i++
Har round ke baad i mein 1 add hoga. Jaise 1, 2, 3...


Code ko step-by-step dekho
Round	i ki value	Condition	Output
1	1	True	1
2	2	True	2
3	3	True	3
4	4	True	4
5	5	True	5
6	6	False	Loop stops
Jab i = 6 ho jata hai, i <= 5 false hota hai aur loop band ho jata hai.
Important: i++ ka matlab i = i + 1 hai.
3. Reverse counting
Agar 5 se 1 tak print karna hai:
for (let i = 5; i >= 1; i--) {
    console.log(i);
}


Output:
5
4
3
2
1


Yahan i-- ka matlab hai har round mein 1 kam karna.
4. while loop
Jab tak condition true hai, loop chalta rahega.
let i: number = 1;

while (i <= 3) {
    console.log(i);
    i++;
}


Output:
1
2
3


Kaise kaam karta hai?
1. i = 1 se start.
2. Condition i <= 3 check hoti hai.
3. Value print hoti hai.
4. i++ value ko badhata hai.
5. Condition false hone par loop stop hota hai.
Warning: Agar i++ hata doge, toh is example mein loop continuously 1 print karta rahega. Isse infinite loop kehte hain.
5. do...while loop
Ismein code pehle execute hota hai, condition baad mein check hoti hai. Isliye loop kam se kam ek baar zaroor chalta hai.
let i: number = 1;

do {
    console.log(i);
    i++;
} while (i <= 3);


Output:
1
2
3


Difference samjho:
let i: number = 10;

while (i <= 3) {
    console.log(i);
}


Output: kuch nahi, kyunki condition shuru mein hi false hai.
Lekin:
let i: number = 10;

do {
    console.log(i);
} while (i <= 3);


Output:
10


Kyunki do...while mein body pehle chalti hai.
6. for...of loop
Is loop ka use arrays ke items ko ek-ek karke access karne ke liye hota hai. Arrays hum agle concept mein detail se seekhenge.
let fruits: string[] = ["Apple", "Mango", "Banana"];

for (const fruit of fruits) {
    console.log(fruit);
}


Output:
Apple
Mango
Banana


Har round mein fruit ko array ka agla item milta hai.

