  TypeScript Lesson 10: type aur interface 🚀
Aaj hum TypeScript ka ek bahut important concept seekhenge: type aur interface.
Inka use objects ka structure define karne ke liye hota hai, taaki TypeScript check kar sake ki data sahi format mein hai ya nahi.
1. Problem samjho
Maan lo tumhare paas multiple employees hain. Har employee ka name, age aur salary hai.
let employee1: {
    name: string;
    age: number;
    salary: number;
} = {
    name: "Rahul",
    age: 25,
    salary: 30000
};

let employee2: {
    name: string;
    age: number;
    salary: number;
} = {
    name: "Priya",
    age: 27,
    salary: 40000
};


Dono objects mein same structure baar-baar likhna pad raha hai.
Solution: type ya interface ka use karo.
2. type kya hota hai?
type se hum ek reusable naam bana sakte hain kisi data structure ke liye.
type Employee = {
    name: string;
    age: number;
    salary: number;
};

let employee1: Employee = {
    name: "Rahul",
    age: 25,
    salary: 30000
};

let employee2: Employee = {
    name: "Priya",
    age: 27,
    salary: 40000
};


Ab Employee ka structure sirf ek baar define kiya.
Samjho:
- type Employee → structure ka naam banaya.
- name: string → name string hona chahiye.
- age: number → age number honi chahiye.
- employee1: Employee → employee1 ko isi structure ko follow karna hoga.
Agar salary missing ho, ya age mein string daal do, to TypeScript error dega.
3. interface kya hota hai?
interface bhi object ka structure define kar sakta hai.
interface Employee {
    name: string;
    age: number;
    salary: number;
}

let employee: Employee = {
    name: "Amit",
    age: 24,
    salary: 35000
};

console.log(employee.name);


Output:
Amit


Yahan interface Employee define karta hai ki Employee object mein kaun-kaun si properties honi chahiye.
4. type aur interface mein difference
Feature	type	interface
Object structure	Yes	Yes
Reuse kar sakte hain	Yes	Yes
Union types	Yes	Directly nahi
Extend karna	Intersection (&) se	extends se
Same name ko dobara declare karna	Generally nahi	Haan, declarations merge ho sakti hain
Beginner level par object structures ke liye dono useful hain. Har situation mein ek hi winner nahi hota.
5. Interface ko extend karna
Maan lo normal employee aur manager dono hain. Manager ke paas employee wali properties ke saath teamSize bhi hai.
interface Employee {
    name: string;
    salary: number;
}

interface Manager extends Employee {
    teamSize: number;
}

let manager: Manager = {
    name: "Rahul",
    salary: 60000,
    teamSize: 5
};

console.log(manager.name);
console.log(manager.teamSize);


Output:
Rahul
5


extends Employee ka matlab hai Manager ko Employee ki properties bhi milengi, aur woh apni extra property bhi define kar sakta hai.
6. Bonus: type ke saath union
type sirf objects ke liye nahi hota. Isse possible values bhi restrict kar sakte hain.
type Status = "pending" | "approved" | "rejected";

let applicationStatus: Status = "pending";

applicationStatus = "approved";


Ye valid hai. Lekin:
applicationStatus = "completed";


TypeScript error dega, kyunki "completed" allowed values mein nahi hai.
Memory trick:
- type → object structure ke saath unions jaise types bhi bana sakta hai.
- interface → objects ka contract define karne ke liye bahut common hai.

